Z||000014||SloPonti||09-12-2000||12:09 AM||||i was not really happy with this show! i took second place in the fiero show in my class! i have a great looking car and there were also some nice ones in my class! the only thing i found to be wrong was that the voting was hard to do! some fieros that did not have nice looking motor or trunk compartments would keep there fieros trunks and hoods down! how can you truly judge a fiero and give an honest oppinion on what looks good and what does not! i think it should be that all fieros in the show should have to have there trunk lids open! other than that the show was great and i met some nice people there-thanks oreif for letting me try out your leather seats! i will be getting those now! and i will be lowering the car now because of the way yours looked! well thanks<BR>Rob<BR>hopped up iron duck!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Haze_Performance||09-12-2000||10:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B>i was not really happy with this show! i took second place in the fiero show in my class! i have a great looking car and there were also some nice ones in my class! the only thing i found to be wrong was that the voting was hard to do! some fieros that did not have nice looking motor or trunk compartments would keep there fieros trunks and hoods down! how can you truly judge a fiero and give an honest oppinion on what looks good and what does not! i think it should be that all fieros in the show should have to have there trunk lids open! other than that the show was great and i met some nice people there-thanks oreif for letting me try out your leather seats! i will be getting those now! and i will be lowering the car now because of the way yours looked! well thanks<BR>Rob<BR>hopped up iron duck!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So, you think that you should of won First Place? Well, it is obvious that your statements are directed towards me, because I came in First. I went there without the expectation to win.  I didn't have my trunk open because I don't like the way the car looks with the trunk open. Although several people did ask what the engine compartment looked like - so I did open it up for them.  (I left my hood open!)  Obviously you spent alot of time detailing your engine compartment, but the sad truth is most people do not notice the engine unless it is a V8 - even though yours looked really good! If you want to get technical, the top three shouldn't have won anything, because we were in the stock class and there were a few very nice bone stock Fiero's there - they are probably upset that they didn't win.  Maybe there needs to be a bettter definition of "stock"?  All in all I thought the show was great - I am glad there was such a good showing of cars, even with the rain! Keep up the good work!<P>Hey Oreif -<BR>Wait until I am in your class next year, I have lots of "juicy" spy photos to compare to!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  lol <BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">      <B>1985 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||8
