Z||000021||Spyro86SE||09-12-2000||04:07 PM||||hey haze you can try my class next year but dont count on it i will beat you i will buy all the votes i can money talks bullsh$t walks money is the root of all evil remember i know where u live if you get out of hand your car may not make it ||||reg||6
Z||000022||SloPonti||09-12-2000||06:35 PM||||hey you better slow down a bit haze!! this was not directed towards you at all!! i counted about a total of 18 fieros there that did not have there trunk open! someone needs a chill pill! further more does your award say first place on it? all of the awards said the same thing o them and nor did they say first place goes to or second place goes to i do not think so-it is also funny that you say that most people don't notice the four cylinders! i get emails every day about my mods and and questions on wheter or not they should do a four cylinder modifications! also somebody very important sure did notice it this weekend-V8 Archie did-there is a nice picture of my motor on his website that he took-that is funny since he deals only in v8-this is not really a true judging car show! it is just what people like! i am used to shows were there are 5-6 judges-thats all i am saying! my car still needs lots of work-i have cracked paint on my mirrors-shaggy seats-but i have a way cool motor and neons and exhaust and stereo! it is all what people like-17 inch wheels make a big difference-but like i said this is not directed towards you so calm down haze-just saying some things that could make the show even better!!!<BR>thanks<BR>hope i did not step on anyones toes here!<BR>Rob <BR>Hopped up Iron Duck||||reg||1
Z||000023||Phil||09-12-2000||07:08 PM||||Personally I never vote for a car that does not have both the hood and trunk open. If it's covered I feel that the owner is hiding something. A lot of experienced show goers feel the same way, yet I see closed cars win over open ones. Some shows now are starting to print up tips for judges which state basicly that if it's hidden assume it's a mess. FWIW (that's why we all show our Fieros with the scratched windows down)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000024||SloPonti||09-12-2000||08:35 PM||||thanks phil-i agree with you totally 100 percent! this should be considered next year at the fierorama show! i will contact the president of the NIFE club and see what he has to say about this!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||6
Z||000025||Phil||09-12-2000||08:44 PM||||Spyro<BR>Just to stir things up a bit - the adage is "The LOVE of money is the root of all evil"||||reg||1
Z||000026||Haze_Performance||09-13-2000||12:23 AM||||Hmmm- So, then Oreif is wrong in his first statement that "Haze and I took First in each of our classes"?  And in your response you said that you took second!! So, does your certificate have second place on it? If not, how do you know that you took second place?? Because Jim stated who took first, second and third places. If you are going to talk to someone in the club about having the trunks open during judging, then apparently you are upset, that according to Jim, I took First Place. I really don't care what place I finish in shows it is just a car show, you are supposed to go to have fun. If you like your car and are happy with what you do with it, that should be all that counts!<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">       <B>1985 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000027||Oreif||09-13-2000||02:03 AM||||First, The certificates given by the club all say the same thing except for what class the car is in to save on expenses. This is also why members pay nothing and there are no Trophy's. It is all for fun. There are 1st, 2nd, and 3rd places. (Yes they did say "first place goes to ....." you'll be able to see/hear it on the video tape) These are also printed up in the club newletter. The objective of it all is to see other fiero's not to argue who's is better. Also the judging is by popular vote of everyone not just a few snobby judges like some car shows I have been to. (No flames against the judges but I have seen a few I thought were very unfair in the way they judged.) I was just as happy the first time I went to a Fierorama and I got 2nd place for my class.<BR> <BR>Second, The Car show is for Daily Driver cars not SHOW CARS. If you noticed all the modified/custom cars had theirs open to display the wonderful engine mods. (Except Archie's Finale which was "V-8 under glass"       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ) The "Display" class isn't even judged! I don't open my decklid because I like the looks of my Indy Scoop. (as well as the large number of people who have asked me numerous questions about it) I have been to many car shows including the large "World of Wheels" and there are people who leave the hoods closed because they are showing off the car with a scoop or other type of modification like paint scheme. Not how much chrome is on the air cleaner. I have been a member for over 4 years now and I can definately say the the N.I.F.E. Board members are all in agreement with how it is set up. In fact the recent newsletter states: "We want to reward you for keeping your Fiero looking great while you drive it, Our awards go to the best kept Fieros with the most mileage, not the showroom new, trailered in Fiero's" <BR>If you want to be "Judged" by a set of rules, The World Of Wheels show is in February.  Again as stated above "IT'S ALL FOR FUN!!"<BR>Sorry it's a long post but I just want everyone to know that the Fierorama is for ALL Fiero's not just "Show Cars"<BR>I'll get off the horse now.       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">      <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||Phil||09-13-2000||07:43 AM||||You will never get "true and equal" judging at any show. Peer  and spectator judging usually means that the people with the most friends attending win. In "expert" judging the judges personal taste enters into the equation. Usually only one person in each class leaves without saying (to themselves at least ) "I was robbed". ||||reg||1
Z||000029||Oreif||09-13-2000||10:31 AM||||Phil, You are correct. I learned that most of the car's that win car shows are the cars where the owner stands by his car and greets everyone and answers questions about the car.<BR>If the car is just sitting there it usually doesn't get a lot of vote's no matter what's been done with it. It's more of a popularity contest than car show. But they are always fun to be at. You meet lots of people with like minded feelings/ideas about the cars and see many very nice cars. I have been to car shows where I didn't win any place and I still enjoyed the show.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Old Lar||09-13-2000||10:55 AM||||I go to the shows to see the other cars.  If I go expecting to get a trophy, I'm usually disappointed.  I have been suprised many times at getting a trophy when there are 5-7 cars that look just like mine and are in competition.  The peer judging is just that.  If I tried to rationalize why I'd get a 1st place for my car in one show, and not get anything in another, I'd go crazy.  I have a lot of trophies at home.  I say spread the wealth around.  There are a lot of nice cars that go to the shows.<P>Actually I like the judging done at Daytona this year where they handed out the judging sheets as to what they were looking at.  I have to admit the defects that were noted are those I knew needed work.  So with that information, I can work on those short comings.  Its just a show.||||reg||5
